        <name>PasswordCrypt</name>
        <qualifiedname>PasswordCrypt::PasswordCrypt</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Initializes libsodium, reporting a critical error (<ref refid="classMessage_1aa085f3b7f644c7c1075eac59e3c2f7a9" kindref="member">Message::CriticalMessage</ref>) on failure. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Ensures libsodium is initialized before any hashing or verification.</para>
<para>libsodium is a library that must be set up once before any of its functions are used; this constructor does that setup. If setup fails, a critical error is logged but the object is still created, so later password operations will simply fail.</para>
<para>A failed initialization is fatal for password operations and is reported through <ref refid="classMessage_1aa085f3b7f644c7c1075eac59e3c2f7a9" kindref="member">Message::CriticalMessage</ref>; construction still succeeds. In everyday words, libsodium needs a one-time &quot;wake up&quot; call before it can be used; this constructor makes that call and shouts in the log if it fails. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
