        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool PasswordCrypt::verifyPassword</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;password, const std::string &amp;hash)</argsstring>
        <name>verifyPassword</name>
        <qualifiedname>PasswordCrypt::verifyPassword</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>password</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>hash</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Verifies <computeroutput>password</computeroutput> against a stored self-describing hash. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Selects the algorithm from the hash prefix: Argon2id (<computeroutput>$argon2...</computeroutput>) or the legacy scrypt format (<computeroutput>$7$</computeroutput>). An unrecognized prefix yields <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> rather than an exception. In everyday words: the stored hash begins with a short label that says which recipe made it. We read that label, run the matching check, and return true only for a real match. Anything we do not understand is safely treated as a failed login, not a crash. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">password</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Plaintext password to check. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">hash</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Stored hash string produced by <ref refid="classPasswordCrypt_1aaa1e7f7eec2be8279ba7330313001546" kindref="member">hashPassword()</ref> or by the legacy scheme. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> only if the password matches the hash; <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> on mismatch, unknown algorithm, or malformed hash.</para>
</simplesect>
Verifies <computeroutput>password</computeroutput> against <computeroutput>hash</computeroutput>, selecting the algorithm from the hash prefix. In everyday words: look at the label at the front of the stored hash to decide which recipe was used, then let libsodium redo the slow mixing and tell us if the result matches. password: Plaintext password. hash: Stored self-describing hash (Argon2id or legacy scrypt). Returns <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> on a match, <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> otherwise (including unknown prefixes). See also: <ref refid="classPasswordCrypt_1aa38216e67e3295979543a5e6a14a4d33" kindref="member">PasswordCrypt::verifyPassword</ref> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
